                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Today with @RepGaramendi I introduced the Medicare IVIG Access Enhancement Act to expand access to home infusion treatments for Medicare beneficiaries with certain conditions requiring intravenous immunoglobulin (IVIG) infusion treatments. Currently, these Americans are at risk because their access to treatment depends on access to an infusion facility.\n\nThis bipartisan bill would make vital in-home IVIG treatments accessible and improve health outcomes for patients living with Chronic Inflammatory Demyelinating Polyneuropathy (CIDP) and Multifocal Motor Neuropathy (MMN).\n\nIn a statement @gbscidp said the organization \u201cwholeheartedly supports this critical piece of legislation that will ensure that patients will be able to access a life-sustaining treatment in their own homes, fixing a longstanding gap in coverage and accessibility for patients with CIDP and MMN.\u201d",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": [
                    "RepGaramendi"
                ],
                "text_tagged_users_ids": [
                    "88806753"
                ],
