                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "The House spent the first half of 2025 working with President Trump to enact big wins for American families \u2013 securing our borders, making tax cuts permanent, ending state Medicaid and SNAP abuses, rebuilding our military, and opening more domestic energy production. Speaker Johnson led our effort to do it all in one bill, and we got the job done.\n\u00a0\nIn September we did our work, passing a clean CR, and Speaker Johnson led our successful efforts to prevent Democrats from forcing through legislation to restore Medicaid for illegal immigrants and ACA credits for the wealthy.\n\u00a0\nSpeaker Johnson's leadership is an important reason we have been successful in passing so many of the President's priorities into law, and I am grateful for his leadership as we continue to put America first every day.",
